WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.175
Protect your bones.

2
00:00:02.215 --> 00:00:05.796
In orbit, they quietly lose strength,
unless you fight back.

3
00:00:07.046 --> 00:00:10.087
Bone is living tissue: it's rebuilt all
the time,

4
00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:12.383
and it adapts to the load it carries.

5
00:00:12.423 --> 00:00:17.044
On Earth, every step you take loads your
bones, and that's what keeps them strong.

6
00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.798
In orbit, your bones no longer carry your
weight.

7
00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:24.769
They lose one to one and a half percent of
their density, every month.

8
00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:29.927
Hips and spine lose the most. Over a
six-month mission, it adds up.

9
00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:33.358
The lost calcium ends up in your urine,

10
00:00:33.358 --> 00:00:36.214
which also raises the risk of kidney
stones.

11
00:00:37.114 --> 00:00:40.929
Your best defense is heavy lifting on the
resistance machine.

12
00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.595
Squats and deadlifts load exactly the
bones that need it.

13
00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:49.622
Eat your full meals, take your vitamin D,
and go easy on salt.

14
00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:54.549
Bone you keep in space is bone you won't
have to rebuild on Earth.

